<Base title="Editorial Policy: How We Write Articles | Grow Revenue"
  description="Who writes the articles on growrevenue.co, how claims and statistics are sourced, how our own data is collected, and how AI tools are used in drafting."
  path="/editorial-policy/" pageType="trust" crumbs={[{ name: 'Editorial policy', path: '/editorial-policy/' }]}>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:20px"><div class="narrow prose">
    <h1 style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,3.2rem)">Editorial policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated October 26, 2026. Every article on growrevenue.co is written and approved by <a href="/kunal-arora/">Kunal Arora</a>, who does the work the articles describe.</p>
    <h2>How do we source claims?</h2>
    <p>Every statistic links to its source within two sentences. Technical rules link to the primary source: Google, Yahoo or Microsoft sender documentation, IETF standards, or the regulator. Where we publish our own data, the article says how it was collected, how many records it covers and the date range.</p>
    <h2>When do we update articles?</h2>
    <p>The published date never changes. The updated date changes only when the text changes in substance, not for small edits. Articles with time-bound facts, such as prices and sender requirements, are re-checked at least every six months and say "as of" the date they were checked.</p>
    <h2>How do we use AI tools?</h2>
    <p>We use AI tools to help research, outline and draft. Every article is then checked against our editorial checklist, fact-checked against its sources and edited by Kunal before it is published. Nothing is published without that review.</p>
    <h2>Do we earn from links?</h2>
    <p>If an article ever contains a link that pays us a commission, it is disclosed above the first such link. Today no article does.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Found an error? Email <a href="mailto:kunal@growrevenue.co">kunal@growrevenue.co</a> and we will correct it and note the correction at the end of the article.</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>
